  "bodyHtml": "\n\n\t\n\t\t<div class=\"archive-header\">\n\n\t<h1 class=\"archive-title\">Image</h1>\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\n</div>\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t<article class=\"entry author-pwsbuilder post-6194 post type-post status-publish format-image category-news\" id=\"post-6194\">\n\n\t<figure class=\"wp-caption center\"><img class=\"size-medium wp-image-6195\" src=\"/media/archive/3fc8ba9d95f7f36c5791b33d27075721f2295d57ca3a87d455edb005bf697eb3.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"667\" height=\"500\" loading=\"lazy\" /><figcaption class=\"wp-caption-text\">\"Guild members Joan Carroll, Phyllis Charles and Karen Shortsleeve took over three artists shacks Saquatucket Harbor to exhibit their work. They were joined by Norm Stafford and the7/7 plein aire artists Larry Folding, Matt Connors and Aaron O'Brien.\"</figcaption></figure>\n\t\n\t\t<header class=\"entry-header\">\n\n\t\t\t<h2 class=\"entry-title\"><a href=\"/news/plein-aire-july-7-2022-at-saquatucket-harbor/\" rel=\"bookmark\">Plein Aire-7/7/2022 at Saquatucket Harbor</a></h2>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"entry-byline\">\n\t\t\t\t<a href=\"/archive/source-ff018cd9606c9d21e3a0/\" class=\"post-format-link\">Image</a>\t\t\t\t<span class=\"entry-author\"><a href=\"/archive/source-37895d34f8cef391272c/\" rel=\"author\" class=\"url fn n\"><span>pwsbuilder</span></a></span>\n\t\t\t\t<time class=\"entry-published updated\" datetime=\"2022-07-13T15:06:04-04:00\" title=\"Wednesday, July 13, 2022, 3:06 pm\">July 13, 2022</time>\n\t\t\t\t<span class=\"comments-link\"></span>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\n\t\t</header>\n\n\t\t<div class=\"entry-summary\">\n\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\n\t\n</article>\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t<article class=\"entry author-pwsbuilder post-6164 post type-post status-publish format-image category-news\" id=\"post-6164\">\n\n\t<figure class=\"wp-caption center\"><img class=\"size-medium wp-image-6166\" src=\"/media/archive/3512afa5f57a5bcdb10052ae1f01e28402fdaef6676815b09d85d933fee327f9.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"667\" height=\"500\" loading=\"lazy\" /><figcaption class=\"wp-caption-text\">Weedie, Katherine Vacca, Mary Shepard, Celince Federici and Donna Tavano are all 'Thursday Open Painting' regulars.</figcaption></figure>\n\t\n\t\t<header class=\"entry-header\">\n\n\t\t\t<h2 class=\"entry-title\"><a href=\"/news/thursday-open-painting-extended/\" rel=\"bookmark\">Thursday Open Painting Extended</a></h2>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"entry-byline\">\n\t\t\t\t<a href=\"/archive/source-ff018cd9606c9d21e3a0/\" class=\"post-format-link\">Image</a>\t\t\t\t<span class=\"entry-author\"><a href=\"/archive/source-37895d34f8cef391272c/\" rel=\"author\" class=\"url fn n\"><span>pwsbuilder</span></a></span>\n\t\t\t\t<time class=\"entry-published updated\" datetime=\"2022-07-01T17:36:18-04:00\" title=\"Friday, July 1, 2022, 5:36 pm\">July 1, 2022</time>\n\t\t\t\t<span class=\"comments-link\"></span>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\n\t\t</header>\n\n\t\t<div class=\"entry-summary\">\n\t\t\t<p>Due to member requests, the Guild’s weekly ‘Thursday Open Painting’ sessions has been extended through the summer.  Sessions take place in the Harwich Community Center from 1pm to 3:30pm. Members are invited to <a href=\"/news/thursday-open-painting-extended/\" class=\"more-link\">[…]</a></p>\n\t\t</div>\n\n\t\n</article>\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t<article class=\"entry author-pwsbuilder post-6155 post type-post status-publish format-image category-news\" id=\"post-6155\">\n\n\t<img src=\"/media/archive/0b35489b95c63c49ac959ebd54723708a29214fd74e0391d708009599527d8e5.png\" loading=\"lazy\" />\n\t\n\t\t<header class=\"entry-header\">\n\n\t\t\t<h2 class=\"entry-title\"><a href=\"/news/6155-2/\" rel=\"bookmark\">ART IN THE PARK</a></h2>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"entry-byline\">\n\t\t\t\t<a href=\"/archive/source-ff018cd9606c9d21e3a0/\" class=\"post-format-link\">Image</a>\t\t\t\t<span class=\"entry-author\"><a href=\"/archive/source-37895d34f8cef391272c/\" rel=\"author\" class=\"url fn n\"><span>pwsbuilder</span></a></span>\n\t\t\t\t<time class=\"entry-published updated\" datetime=\"2022-06-30T16:36:52-04:00\" title=\"Thursday, June 30, 2022, 4:36 pm\">June 30, 2022</time>\n\t\t\t\t<span class=\"comments-link\"></span>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\n\t\t</header>\n\n\t\t<div class=\"entry-summary\">\n\t\t\t<p>   For Art and Community PRESS RELEASE FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE Date: June 28, 2022 Submitted by Michael Rudden, President RE:  Guild of Harwich Artists – Mondays Art-in-the-Park Starts July 4th <a href=\"/news/6155-2/\" class=\"more-link\">[…]</a></p>\n\t\t</div>\n\n\t\n</article>\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t<article class=\"entry author-pwsbuilder post-6111 post type-post status-publish format-image has-post-thumbnail category-news\" id=\"post-6111\">\n\n\t<img class=\"alignnone size-medium wp-image-6125\" src=\"/media/archive/54123f85af30bd0ea28d7cc87a1af51a15e0cda0790ed8b6878bf7def53c5554.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"292\" height=\"300\" loading=\"lazy\" />\n\t\n\t\t<header class=\"entry-header\">\n\n\t\t\t<h2 class=\"entry-title\"><a href=\"/news/cooperative-bank-show-april-22-2022/\" rel=\"bookmark\">Cooperative Bank Show April 22, 2022</a></h2>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"entry-byline\">\n\t\t\t\t<a href=\"/archive/source-ff018cd9606c9d21e3a0/\" class=\"post-format-link\">Image</a>\t\t\t\t<span class=\"entry-author\"><a href=\"/archive/source-37895d34f8cef391272c/\" rel=\"author\" class=\"url fn n\"><span>pwsbuilder</span></a></span>\n\t\t\t\t<time class=\"entry-published updated\" datetime=\"2022-04-22T17:44:49-04:00\" title=\"Friday, April 22, 2022, 5:44 pm\">April 22, 2022</time>\n\t\t\t\t<span class=\"comments-link\"></span>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\n\t\t</header>\n\n\t\t<div class=\"entry-summary\">\n\t\t\t<p>Thank you all Guild members that attended last night’s reception at the first after hours reception at the Coopertive bank in East Harwich! In attendance were Larry, “Weedie,” Katherine Vacca, <a href=\"/news/cooperative-bank-show-april-22-2022/\" class=\"more-link\">[…]</a></p>\n\t\t</div>\n\n\t\n</article>\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t<article class=\"entry author-pwsbuilder post-5848 post type-post status-publish format-image category-news\" id=\"post-5848\">\n\n\t<img class=\"alignnone size-medium wp-image-5849\" src=\"/media/archive/ce219c394f47e2c7fa58948e5836c3d21488689360e9ef300372cbd4c8ea0d8c.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"300\" height=\"225\" loading=\"lazy\" />\n\t\n\t\t<header class=\"entry-header\">\n\n\t\t\t<h2 class=\"entry-title\"><a href=\"/news/the-cooperative-bank-show-winter-2022/\" rel=\"bookmark\">The Cooperative Bank Show – Winter 2022</a></h2>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"entry-byline\">\n\t\t\t\t<a href=\"/archive/source-ff018cd9606c9d21e3a0/\" class=\"post-format-link\">Image</a>\t\t\t\t<span class=\"entry-author\"><a href=\"/archive/source-37895d34f8cef391272c/\" rel=\"author\" class=\"url fn n\"><span>pwsbuilder</span></a></span>\n\t\t\t\t<time class=\"entry-published updated\" datetime=\"2022-01-22T16:57:08-05:00\" title=\"Saturday, January 22, 2022, 4:57 pm\">January 22, 2022</time>\n\t\t\t\t<span class=\"comments-link\"></span>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\n\t\t</header>\n\n\t\t<div class=\"entry-summary\">\n\t\t\t<p>     New show at the Cooperative Bank in East Harwich. Come and meet the staff. Chris Caltaldo is the Bank Manager and Carrol Bradley is the Assistant Branch Manager.  <a href=\"/news/the-cooperative-bank-show-winter-2022/\" class=\"more-link\">[…]</a></p>\n\t\t</div>\n\n\t\n</article>\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t<article class=\"entry author-pwsbuilder post-5758 post type-post status-publish format-image category-news\" id=\"post-5758\">\n\n\t<img class=\"aligncenter size-medium wp-image-5696\" src=\"/media/archive/24c98517c89b5272adfb274bc119ee008d1861dc3c9fd58bcbc4d0d6a066dfb0.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"300\" height=\"158\" loading=\"lazy\" />\n\t\n\t\t<header class=\"entry-header\">\n\n\t\t\t<h2 class=\"entry-title\"><a href=\"/news/one-more-round/\" rel=\"bookmark\">One More Round!</a></h2>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"entry-byline\">\n\t\t\t\t<a href=\"/archive/source-ff018cd9606c9d21e3a0/\" class=\"post-format-link\">Image</a>\t\t\t\t<span class=\"entry-author\"><a href=\"/archive/source-37895d34f8cef391272c/\" rel=\"author\" class=\"url fn n\"><span>pwsbuilder</span></a></span>\n\t\t\t\t<time class=\"entry-published updated\" datetime=\"2021-05-11T08:19:03-04:00\" title=\"Tuesday, May 11, 2021, 8:19 am\">May 11, 2021</time>\n\t\t\t\t<span class=\"comments-link\"></span>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\n\t\t</header>\n\n\t\t<div class=\"entry-summary\">\n\t\t\t<p>After successfully gathering over 80 member-created “sunshine cards” that Council on Aging distributed for Valentine’s Day and Easter/Spring, can we do it one last time for Memorial Day? The COA <a href=\"/news/one-more-round/\" class=\"more-link\">[…]</a></p>\n\t\t</div>\n\n\t\n</article>\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\t<nav class=\"navigation pagination\" aria-label=\"Posts pagination\">\n\t\t<h2 class=\"screen-reader-text\">Posts pagination</h2>\n\t\t<div class=\"nav-links\"><span class=\"page-numbers current\">1</span>\n<a class=\"page-numbers\" title=\"Archived control; this function is not available here\" href>2</a><span data-fidelity-note=\"functional\" class=\"note\"> (archived control)</span>\n<a class=\"next page-numbers\" title=\"Archived control; this function is not available here\" href>Next →</a><span data-fidelity-note=\"functional\" class=\"note\"> (archived control)</span></div>\n\t</nav>\n\n\t\n",
